"""
Real-time pulse extraction using the POS algorithm.

pos_algorithm(), bandpass_filter(), estimate_heart_rate(), and all of the
MediaPipe-based face/skin ROI extraction (landmarks_to_pixels,
build_roi_mask, mean_skin_rgb, build_face_landmarker,
ensure_face_landmarker_model) are copied VERBATIM and never touched by
any of the tracker/diagnostics work below.

# ===== KCF TRACKER CHANGE =====
Default tracker changed from MOSSE to KCF. The tracker/orchestration
layer (FaceROITracker) now also:
  - explicitly verifies KCF availability at startup instead of assuming
    it (§3), with a big, unmissable banner if it's missing,
  - labels every re-detection with a specific reason code (§10) so
    "tracker never engages" (unavailable) can be told apart from
    "tracker engages but fails immediately" (update() False) from
    "tracker succeeds but gets geometrically rejected",
  - never permanently disables itself after a single runtime failure
    (only after a hard capability check fails at startup) (§5/§6).
# ===== PERFORMANCE DIAGNOSTICS =====
The per-second HR summary now prints the full 10-second-window block
format requested (MediaPipe/KCF frame counts, usage %, re-detections,
tracker failures, capture-vs-nominal FPS), and a final end-of-run
performance summary is printed on exit. All of this is diagnostic
printing layered around the exact same unmodified pos_algorithm /
bandpass_filter / estimate_heart_rate calls as before -- the actual
HR math is untouched.

Requires: pip install mediapipe opencv-python scipy numpy
(opencv-contrib-python required for KCF/MOSSE trackers)
"""

